{"chunk_id": "58bfbe406ae0", "text": "This section recounts the origins and rise of the great Rakshasa figures tied to the Ramayana. The brothers Ravana, Kumbhakarna, and Vibhishana\u2014sons of Visrava\u2014perform terrible austerities to obtain boons from Brahma after envying the wealth of Kuvera. Ravana\u2019s extreme penance, including offering his own heads into the sacred fire, wins him near invulnerability against gods and supernatural beings, though he arrogantly ignores the threat of humans. Kumbhakarna receives the strange boon of prolonged sleep, while the righteous Vibhishana asks only for unwavering adherence to dharma and is granted immortality. Empowered, Ravana conquers Lanka from Kuvera and terrorizes the worlds. Alarmed sages appeal to Brahma, who reveals that Vishnu will incarnate to destroy Ravana, while the gods will be born on earth as monkeys and bears to aid him.\nRavana and his siblings perform severe austerities, receive boons from Brahma, Ravana rises to power and oppresses the worlds, prompting the gods to plan Vishnu\u2019s incarnation.\nThemes: ascetic austerities, boons and curses, rise of Ravana, divine intervention plan, fate through overlooked weakness", "vector": [0.005624132230877876, -0.029632888734340668, 0.008013114333152771, -0.011635666713118553, -0.012893025763332844, 0.01379016786813736, -0.015278609469532967, -0.02246934175491333, -0.025500597432255745, -0.012172592803835869, 0.004159478936344385, 0.004329392220824957, 0.01953323930501938, 0.007537356577813625, -0.008781122043728828, 0.010928827337920666, 0.03670128434896469, -0.0221702940762043, 0.028790120035409927, -0.011057961732149124, -0.003510409966111183, 0.002997271716594696, -0.008978221565485, 0.007788828108459711, -0.028572630137205124, 0.0038094574119895697, 0.01826908439397812, -0.03395548462867737, 0.016841812059283257, -0.007496577221900225, -0.012811467051506042, -0.012050255201756954, 0.006021729204803705, 0.0018316659843549132, -0.022496528923511505, 0.0